1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,950
A gene can have more than two alleles in a population, although each person carries only two.

2
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:11,341
The ABO blood group gene has three: I A, I B and little i.

3
00:00:11,341 --> 00:00:17,213
I A and I B are codominant with each other, and both are dominant over i.

4
00:00:17,213 --> 00:00:20,481
That gives six genotypes and four blood groups.

